============================================================

Implement a rule engine that consumes normalized differences.

Each finding must contain:

- Unique rule ID
- Title
- Category
- Severity
- Confidence
- Summary
- Evidence
- Recommendation
- False-positive considerations
- References where appropriate

Initial categories:

- protocol
- status
- headers
- cookies
- body
- reflection
- redirect
- caching
- cors
- authentication
- authorization
- information-disclosure
- transport-security
- content-security

Initial severities:

- info
- low
- medium
- high

Do not implement critical severity in the first release.

Example rule identifiers:

HTTPDIFF-HEADER-001
HTTPDIFF-COOKIE-001
HTTPDIFF-CACHE-001
HTTPDIFF-REFLECT-001
HTTPDIFF-AUTHZ-001
HTTPDIFF-REDIRECT-001

Keep rules modular and testable.

Rules should not be hardcoded into presentation code.

Use a structure such as:

httpdiff/rules/
  base.py
