26. SECURITY AND PRIVACY
============================================================

The tool may process credentials, cookies, tokens, personal information, and private response bodies.

Implement secure defaults:

- Redact secrets
- Do not transmit telemetry
- Do not upload data
- Do not make external requests except user-requested target requests
- Do not log full credentials
- Do not expose Authorization or Cookie values in errors
- Clearly warn when --show-secrets is used
- Avoid writing reports with secrets unless explicitly enabled

Include a SECURITY.md file explaining responsible vulnerability reporting for HTTPDiff itself.

============================================================
27. LIMITATIONS
============================================================

Document that the first release:

- Does not prove that a vulnerability exists
- Does not replace manual testing
- Does not execute JavaScript
- Does not parse raw HTTP/2 frames
- Does not automatically discover cache keys
- Does not crawl websites
- Does not exploit findings
- May produce false positives
- May miss application-specific authorization semantics
- Cannot infer user intent from response text alone

